{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"Swidux","externalID":"Swidux","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux is a Redux-style state-management library for SwiftUI. State lives in one observable store, mutations go through reducers, and side effects run as async effects. Macros generate the observability boilerplate. Built-in plugins handle persistence and undo\/redo. Four optional plugins ship ready-made paywalls (RevenueCat or StoreKit-shaped), version killswitches, parental gates, and analytics (Mixpanel or any backend).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The dispatch cycle:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["View → store.send(.action)","  → willReduce hooks (UndoPlugin snapshots here)","  → reducer mutates state in place, optionally returns Effect","  → plugin reducers handle their own actions","  → afterReduce hooks (PersistencePlugin drains EntityStore changelogs here)","  → observer tree updates only changed properties (per-property observation)","  → effects run on a background actor; results dispatch back via @MainActor send"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Your domain types and database stay in your app. Swidux provides the contracts, observability, and dispatch loop.","type":"text"}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFir